Elarique Swiftblade.wikitext:
{{EldarPortal}}
'''Elarique Swiftblade''' is a female [[Eldar]] from [[Craftworld]] [[Alaitoc]]{{Fn|1a}} who eventually took the title of [[Autarch]].{{Fn|1b}} She is known to have held a great deal of enmity towards the [[Chaos]] [[Sorceror]] [[Ygethmor]].{{Fn|1a}} During the [[Thirteenth Black Crusade]], a [[Warp Storm]] was heading towards the planet [[Medusa V]] that contained a portal into the [[Webway]]. The [[Farseer]]s foretold that Alaitoc would suffer the most as the [[Warp]] would pollute the Webway and that [[Daemon]]s would corrupt the [[Infinity Circuit]] of the Craftworld.{{Fn|1a}}

As a result, Autarch Swiftblade assembled the forces of a dozen Craftworlds with the intention of conducting a ritual to seal the portal into the Webway located on Medusa V before the Warp Storm engulfed the planet. However, only the closest to Elarique Swiftblade know that her arch-nemesis Ygethmor resided on the world and it is believed that she would gamble with the fate of her Craftworld in order to get her revenge on the Sorceror.{{Fn|1a}}

Ultimately, the Eldar managed to close the portal but at heavy loss which included the death of Autarch Swiftblade who died but not before beheading Ygethmor though she was slain by his bodyguard in turn.{{Fn|a}}

==Notes==
*{{Endn|a}}: The character makes an appearance in [[The Fall of Medusa V]] campaign, with her fate being published on the [[Games Workshop]] website after the completion of the campaign.

