Elion.wikitext:
{{UltramarinesPortal}}
[[File:Lyreo,Altareus,Elion.jpg|thumb|right|250px|[[Altareus]], [[Lyreo]], and Elion (right) standing before [[Demetrian Titus|Titus]]{{Fn|1a}}]]
'''Elion''' was an [[Intercessor]] in the [[Ultramarines]]' [[Combat Squad Damocles]], which was part of the [[Chapter]]'s [[2nd Company (Ultramarines)|2nd Company]].{{Fn|1a}}
==History==
{{Spoiler|source=Space Marine II}}
The [[Combat Squad Damocles|Squad]] was originally under the command of [[Space Marine Sergeant|Sergeant]] [[Gadriel]], when the [[2nd Company (Ultramarines)|2nd Company]] aided in the defense of the [[Tyranid]] invaded [[Recidious System]]. However after [[Demetrian Titus]] was reinstated into the [[Ultramarines]] as a [[Space Marine Lieutenant|Lieutenant]], the [[Company]]'s [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]], [[Sevastus Acheran]], gave Titus command of Damocles. He then charged the Squad with re-securing the [[Orbital Defence Cannon]]s on [[Kadaku]], which had been swarmed by Tyranids, so that the [[Imperial]] forces in the [[System]] could finish the evacuation of the doomed world. The [[Cadian 8th]] had been tasked with protecting the Cannons, until the Tyranids began overwhelming them and the [[Regiment]] was forced to retreat. When the [[Thunderhawk]] [[Absolver (Thunderhawk)|Absolver]], deployed the Squad at the Cadians' new location, they met with [[Major]] [[Sarkaana]] who informed them of the situation.{{Fn|1a}} 

Upon learning that the [[Tyranids]] were continuing to launch assaults against the [[Regiment]], [[Demetrian Titus|Titus]] charged  the [[Combat Squad Damocles|Squad]] member [[Lyreo]] with helping the [[Cadian 8th]] secure their location, with the aid of Elion and [[Altareus]]. The [[Space Marine Lieutenant|Lieutenant]], meanwhile would take [[Gadriel]] and [[Chairon]] to reclaim the [[Orbital Defence Cannon]]s. Once the area was secure, though, the three were to rejoin Titus and aid in reclaiming the Cannons as well. However before they could do so, [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Sevastus Acheran]] gave Lyreo, Altareus and Elion new orders to carry out on [[Kadaku]]. The [[Intercessor]] informed Titus of this and stated the Lieutenant's group would have to reclaim the Cannons on their own.{{Fn|1a}} As they carried out their Captain's orders, though, the three were swarmed by [[Hormagaunt]]s and Elion became separated from the others. After Altareus and Lyreo defeated the Tyranids, they discovered that he had been killed during the battle. Some type of Tyranid had put a hole clean through Elion's head, which a sorrowful Lyreo shared with Titus after both of their missions had been completed.{{Fn|1b}}

When [[Gadriel]] heard of Elion's death, he was shocked and angered, as the two had fought together for twenty years. The [[Space Marine Sergeant|Sergeant]] told [[Lyreo]] that he should have been there fighting besides them and could not believe that Elion was killed by [[Hormagaunt]]s. When [[Demetrian Titus]] stated that there were far more [[Lictor|deadly creatures]] on [[Kadaku]], Gadriel directed his anger at the [[Space Marine Lieutenant|Lieutenant]]. He blamed Titus for Elion's death and said the Lieutenant should not have divided the [[Combat Squad Damocles|Squad]], during the mission. Titus stoically replied that Elion was gone and their duty to the [[Imperium]] was all. Gadriel angerily responded that he does not forget his [[Battle Brother|brothers]], as the Lieutenant did.{{Fn|1b}} 

