Eliphas.wikitext:
{{CSMPortal}}
'''Eliphas the Inheritor''' was the [[Dark Apostle]] leading the [[Word Bearers]] on [[Kronus]] during the [[Dark Crusade]]. While thought to have been killed at the end of that campaign, he returned during the [[Second Aurelian Crusade]] as a champion of the [[Black Legion]].

He got his name from ascending in rank by killing his predecessor. When [[Primarch]] [[Lorgar]] saw this, he said Eliphas moved up in rank, inheriting the position, rather than having truly earned it.{{Fn|4}}

==History==
===Horus Heresy===
During the very latest phases of the [[Shadow Crusade]], Eliphas and his [[Ark of Testimony]] [[Chapter (Word Bearers)|Chapter]] invaded the world of [[Kronus]] with the help of a contingent of [[World Eaters]]. There he built a mighty temple to [[Chaos]]: the [[Templum Daemonarchia]], seeking to gain favour from [[Lorgar]]. They set up an ambush for [[Ultramarines]], sacrificing them as well as any dead from their own side to the [[Warp]] as the battle went on. Lorgar was ultimately unimpressed by Eliphas.{{Fn|4}}

===The Dark Crusade===
[[Image:Eliphas_DOWDC.jpeg|right|thumb|250px|Eliphas at the beginning of Dark Crusade.]]
During the opening phases of the [[Dark Crusade]], Eliphas and the Word Bearers were summoned back to Kronus by a [[Chaos cult]] at the Third Temple of Black Succession in the far south of the Deimos Peninsula.{{Fn|1a}} This cabal had turned to Chaos in light of their experiences with the recent rise of the [[Necron]]s on Kronus, and Eliphas had answered. Using the knowledge gained from the [[Book of the Epistles of Lorgar]], their leader [[Virgilius]] planned to bring Eliphas to Kronus. On the eighth night of their visit to the Temple, Virgilius led them to the great chamber at the temple's heart, where he and eight of his cultists were sacrificed on an icon of Chaos. The [[Warp]] opened between the points of the eight-pointed star and Eliphas stepped forth, heralding the beginning of the Ninth Inheritance.{{Fn|1k}}

Eliphas came to Kronus to turn the planet into a [[Daemon World]]{{Fn|1i}}, and would go on to lead the Word Bearers against the other six factions all vying for supremacy on the planet. He began his conquest from the Daemon Gate situated in the Deimos Peninsula on the tropical southern coast of Kronus. Of all the powers on Kronus, barring the [[Blood Ravens]] of the [[Adeptus Astartes]] he despised the [[Necron]]s most as they had no souls to be devoured by his gods.{{Fn|1a}}

He was armed with an [[Accursed Crozius]] and over the course of the conflict, gained new equipment to enhance his powers, such as Daemonic Armour and the same helm worn by the Word Bearers [[Primarch]] [[Lorgar]] 10,000 years previously during the Horus Heresy.{{Fn|1h}}

[[Image:Eliphas Inheritor.jpg|right|thumb|250px|Eliphas the Inheritor.]]
Throughout the Dark Crusade, Eliphas was given ample opportunity to gain favour with the four [[Chaos Gods]] and other Chaos figures through the defeat of his enemies.
*[[Khorne]]'s by offering to him the skull of Lord [[Crull]], a champion of the Blood God slain by [[Warboss]] [[Gorgutz 'Ead 'Unter]].{{Fn|1b}}
*[[Slaanesh]]'s by cracking open all the [[spirit stone]]s left behind when the [[Eldar]] fled Tyrea, and offering the souls within to the Prince of Excess.{{Fn|1c}}
*[[Nurgle]]'s by freeing the Plague Daemon imprisoned within the [[Aquila Ignis|Hellstorm Cannon]] in Victory Bay, using the rotting corpses of the [[Imperial Guard|Imperial]] [[Guardsman|Guardsmen]] as sacrifice.{{Fn|1d}}
*[[Tzeentch]]'s by defeating the Necron army beneath the Thur'Abis plateau.{{Fn|1e}}
*[[Warmaster]] [[Ezekyle Abaddon|Abaddon's]] by defeating the [[Blood Ravens]] in North Vandea, although it is unknown why the defeat of a chapter whose history does not date back to the Horus Heresy would be especially pleasing to Abaddon.{{Fn|1f}}
*Word Bearers Primarch Lorgar's, said to hate the irreligious above all others, by defeating the [[Tau]] forces in Or'es Tash'n.{{Fn|1g}}

Deimos was eventually conquered by the Blood Ravens.{{Fn|2}} Eliphas was last seen trying to explain his failure to an unnamed [[Daemon Prince]]. The Daemon Prince declared that Eliphas was past redemption and refused to send him to the [[Basilica of Torments]] again, opting to destroy him outright instead, claiming that ''"It is a poor shepherd who blames his flock, Apostle. This failure is yours and yours alone."'' Eliphas attacked the Daemon Prince, but was lifted into the air by the Prince's power, and exploded in a huge gush of blood.{{Fn|1j}}

===Chaos Rising===
Eliphas reappeared as a champion for the [[Black Legion]] against the [[Blood Ravens]] on planet [[Aurelia]], having been somehow resurrected.{{Fn|2a}} He led a warband together with [[Araghast the Pillager]]{{Fn|2b}}, but later deserted him, causing [[Araghast]]'s death and leaving Eliphas as sole commander of the warband.{{Fn|2c}} He was later defeated by the Blood Raven [[Aramus]].{{Fn|2d}} As punishment, Eliphas was tortured by [[Abaddon the Despoiler]], promising through his pain that he would succeed in corrupting the Blood Ravens.{{Fn|2e}}

===Retribution===
Eliphas returned during the [[Aurelian Crusades|Third Aurelian Crusade]], this time in [[Terminator Armour]]. He was sent by Abaddon to claim the souls of the Blood Ravens and the population of [[Subsector Aurelia]].{{Fn|3a}}

==Trivia==
