Eloise Athagey.wikitext:
{{ImperialNavyPortal}}
'''Eloise Athagey''' was the [[Groupmaster]] of [[Indomitus Crusade Fleet Tertius]]' [[Battle Group Saint Aster]] and a [[Commodore]] in the [[Imperial Navy]].{{Fn|1}}

==History==
[[Image:Athagey.jpg|thumb|right|220px|{{PAGENAME}}{{Fn|1a}}]]
Athagey was the fourteenth daughter of a prominent Imperial Navy [[Admiral]]. Their family is a rich noble house on [[Armageddon]].{{Fn|3c}}

Originally commanding an Imperial Navy flotilla defending [[Fomor III]], Athagey soon joined the [[Indomitus Crusade Fleet Tertius]] under [[Fleetmaster]] [[Cassandra VanLeskus]].{{Fn|1b}} During the [[Battle of the Machorta Sound]] Athagey led Battle Group Saint Aster against the [[Khornate]] [[Blackstone]] device from the [[Overlord Class Battlecruiser]] ''[[Saint Aster (Battle Cruiser)|Saint Aster]]''. She narrowly survived the battle after the bridge of the ''Saint Aster'' was boarded by [[Daemons]], surviving only thanks to her [[Rogal Dorn|Dorn]]-descended [[Unnumbered Sons]] bodyguards and the sabotaging of the enemy Blackstone machine thanks to the efforts of [[Captain]] [[Messinius]] and [[Inquisitor]] [[Rostov]].{{Fn|1c}}

Later during a meeting with [[Fabian Guelphrain]], Athagey expressed extreme bitterness towards Guilliman and the Imperial leadership in general with what she saw as her battlegroup and legacy of the Saint Aster being subordinated to [[Battle Group Iolus]], as well as Fabian's perceived role as Guilliman's spy. After a seemingly intoxicated rant, Fabian suspects Athagey may be abusing [[Stimm]]s.{{Fn|2}}

Despite her addiction, Athagey later proved a key Imperial commander during the first major battle of the [[Pariah Crusade]]. She arrived at [[Paradyce II]] finding [[Fleetmaster]] [[VanLeskus]] dead and Fleet Tertius in disarray. Ignoring her desire to use Stimms to take command of the situation, Athagey was able to ram her flagship ''[[Saint Aster (Battle Cruiser)|Saint Aster]]'' into the Necron [[Pylon ship]], destroying it and allowing for the surviving Imperial ships to escape.{{Fn|3a}} However in the aftermath Athagey along with much of her crew were captured by the Necron [[Phaeron]] [[Zhulkan]], an emissary of the [[Silent King]] [[Szarekh]].{{Fn|3b}}

