Emeric (Castellan).wikitext:
{{BlackTemplarsPortal}}
'''Emeric''' is a [[Black Templars]] [[Castellan (Black Templars)|Castellan]] in the [[Second Dorean Crusade]], who commands the warship [[Dauntless Honour]].{{Fn|1a}}  

==History==
During the Crusade, the Templar forces under Castellan suffered heavy losses including the death of its [[Marshal (Black Templars)|Marshal]] [[Arold]]. As Emeric reflected on this, the ship experienced a [[Gellar Field]] disruption which caused [[Daemon]]s to possess the [[Astropath]]s. The ''Dauntless Honour'' was forced from the warp as Emeric and his Templars slew though possessed. Emeric was informed that the [[Navigator]] was comatose and the ''Dauntless Honour'' is critically damaged. He then commanded the ship limp toward the nearby [[Shrine World]] of [[Tempest]].{{Fn|1a}}

Shortly after, the ''Dauntless Honour'' recieved a distress call from a nearby Templars vessel, the ''Spiteful Blade'', giving them new hope. After boarding the vessel, they discover the crew mutilated and learn it was overrun by Daemons. The only survivor was the [[Neophyte]] [[Juerten]], and Emeric ordered the reactor of the ''Spiteful Blade'' overloaded to cleanse it by causing a massive explosion. Amongst those left behind was Juerten, who was deemed corrupted.{{Fn|1b}}

The ''Dauntless Honour'' was eventually able to reach Tempest, finding the main Crusade Fleet has arrived arrived and is now under siege by [[Chaos]] forces led by the [[World Eaters]] [[Possessed Chaos Space Marine]] [[Dravek Soulrender]]. Emeric, now with less than 40 Battle-Brothers, all take an oath to cleanse the world of heretics.{{Fn|1b}}

Breaking the traitor blockade and landing on Tempest, Emeric and his forces joined a group of [[Frateris Militia]] resistance groups and established a small base at the city of Saint Ciubrus after purging it of Chaos forces. They then decided to use the worlds catacombs to reach the Shrine of Saint Iglese to relieve the defenders there.{{Fn|1c}} At the Shrine, the Templars discovered the corrupt [[Priest]]s to have simply hunkered down and not waged any kind of defense. Emeric forced those inside to action, destroying the gates and forbidding any retreat.They then marched towards the capital of Saint Ofelias, the site of the main siege by the Soulrender's army.{{Fn|1d}}

In the battle at Saint Ofelias, Emeric and his army arrived just as the city was about to be overrun. They were able to fight their way to the Cathedral of the Martyr as a monstrous [[Daemon Engine]] appears. Realizing they can't fight it head-on, Emeric and a dozen of his remaining brothers launch a boarding operation on the machine. Taking heavy losses, Emeric used his Crusade's last [[Thunderhawk]] in a kamikaze attack, finally taking it down.{{Fn|1e}} The Daemon engine's destruction creates a localized [[Warp]] storm which the Imperials, now led by Emeric and just four other Templars, use to try and retreat back to the ''Dauntless Honour''.{{Fn|1f}}

In the final battle, Soulrender, now fully possessed by his Daemon named [[The Carver]], attacks the ''Dauntless Honour''. The Imperials make their last stand and all of Emeric's remaining brothers are killed. In a final act of defiance Emeric is able to kill Soulrender and banish The Carver by strangling him.{{Fn|1f}} The sole survivor of the Crusade, Emeric was eventually discovered by Marshal [[Laise]], who revealed he had once been his former apprence. The main Crusade fleet arrived and Emeric, now with a mechanical arm and leg, reflected on the sacrifice of his brothers and realizes his true purpose had simply been to hold the line rather than win a decisive battle himself.{{Fn|1g}}

