Enoch (Princeps).wikitext:
{{CollegiaTitanicaPortal}}
{{otheruses|USE=Princeps|OTHERPAGE=Enoch (disambiguation)}}
[[Princeps]] '''Enoch''' commanded the [[Warlord Titan]] ''[[Invictus (Titan)|Invictus]]'' of the [[Legio Astraman]] during the [[Graia (History)|invasion]] of the [[Forge World]] [[Graia]] by both [[Ork]] and [[Chaos]] forces. During the initial Ork invasion, the power to [[Manufactorium Ajakis]], where the ''Invictus'' was berthed, was disrupted preventing the Titan's release from its mooring clamps. Enoch and his crew could do nothing as the Orks rampaged across the Forge World. This continued for some time until after the subsequent [[Chaos]] invasion, as [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Titus (Ultramarines)|Titus]] of the [[Ultramarines]] and his squad fought their way through the Manufactorium to the Titan and engaged its back up generator.{{Fn|1a}}

Titus explained to Enoch that he needed the ''Invictus'' to fire upon the Forge World's Orbital Tower, where the [[Chaos Lord]] [[Nemeroth]] was opening a [[Warp]] Gate big enough to allow his fleet to enter through. In order to do this Titus needed to place the Power Source, created by [[Inquisitor]] [[Drogan]], into ''Invictus'' to power up its weapons enough to do the job. Enoch was hesitant at first because of the breach of protocol, until Titus convinced him of the severity of the situation{{Fn|1a}}. With reluctance he showed Titus where to place the Power Source and with the ''Invictus''' power increased he fired upon the Orbital Tower, partially destroying it and closing Nemeroth's Warp Gate. The firing of its weapon, overloaded the systems of the ''Invictus'' and with confirmation that they had succeeded, Enoch powered down the Titan.{{Fn|1b}}

==Sources==
*1: [[Warhammer 40,000: Space Marine]]
**{{Endn|1a}}: Chapter 13: Waking the Sleeping Giant
**{{Endn|1b}}: Chapter 14: Victory and Sacrifice

