Eon Kull.wikitext:
{{EldarPortal}}
'''Eon Kull''' was an [[Aeldari]] [[Farseer]] of [[Craftworld]] [[Dolthe]].{{Fn|1}}


==Biography==
Even by the standards of the long-lived Aeldari, Eon Kull was ancient, to the point that some knew him simply as '''The Old One'''.{{Fn|1}}

While the [[Sabbat Worlds Crusade]] was waged in [[Segmentum Pacificus]], Kull led an Aeldari warhost to the planet [[Monthax]], planning to enact a ritual to close a [[Webway Portal]] there, fearing that the [[Chaos]] forces active on Monthax would use it to invade Dolthe. In order to defend the portal while the ritual was being performed, Kull conjured a storm to obscure the ruins and stymie their enemies. However, the storm was far greater in magnitude than he had intended and as a result the [[Astra Militarum]] fighting against the Chaos forces on Monthax suffered horrendous casualties. Eventually the strain of the ritual proved too much for Kull and he perished, but the portal was still sealed thanks to the help of [[Inquisitor]] [[Lilith Abfequarn]].{{Fn|1}}

==Wargear==
Eon Kull's armaments included the [[witchblade]] ''[[Fuehain Falchior]]''. At one point he also wielded the [[Shrieker Cannon|shrieker cannon]] ''[[Uliowye]]''; while on Monthax he gave the cannon to his chief bodyguard, the [[Dire Avenger]] [[Muon Nol]].{{Fn|1}}


==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
===Conflicting sources===
At one point the source claims that Eon Kull is a [[Warlock]], however Kull calls himself a Farseer.{{Fn|1}}

