Epsilus Dammek-Yoth.wikitext:
{{AdeptusMechanicusPortal}}
[[Image:Epsilus.jpeg|thumb|right|220px|Epsilus Dammek-Yoth{{Fn|3a}}]]
'''Epsilus Dammek-Yoth''' is an [[Heretek|Arch-Heretek]] and [[Xenarite]] from the [[Forge World]] [[Stygies VIII]]{{Fn|1a}}, who wields the master-crafted [[Power Axe]], '''The Sufferer Shattering Axe'''.{{Fn|2}}

Epsilus was once a researcher into xenobiology and a pioneer of research on the [[Necrons]], eventually rising to the rank of [[Archmagos]] Veneratus. Much of the information [[Faustinius]] uses to assess the Necron threat on [[Silva Tenebris]] comes from Epsilus. In time, Epsilus came to believe that the Necrons technology should be used to help first the [[Adeptus Mechanicus]] and then mankind entire to discard their flesh and humanity. Fleeing Stygies VIII after a purge of Xenarites within their ranks, Epsilus has gone into hiding and seeks to further his heresy in defiance of both the Machine-Cult and the Imperial Creed.{{Fn|3a}}

He infiltrated the [[Ark Mechanicus]] ''[[Caestus Metalican]]'', when [[Magos Dominus]] [[Faustinius]] took command of it and led an expedition to the world [[Silva Tenebris]]. When it was revealed that Tenebris was actually a [[Necron Tomb World]], Epsilus used [[Tech-Priests]] that he had corrupted to stage an uprising aboard the ''Caestus''{{Fn|1a}}, in order to claim the Necrons' xenotech.{{Fn|2}}

Epsilus briefly managed to seize control of the starboard gunnery deck of the ''Caestus Metalican''. However, his forces were defeated by loyal [[Skitarii]]. Epsilus briefly attempted to negotiate with Faustinius, offering to spare him and his supporters if he voluntarily turned control of the vessel and the expedition over to Epsilus.{{Fn|1b}}

Epsilus was eventually cornered and slain by Faustinius' tech-priests before he could complete his plot. All evidence of his existence was expunged and all his followers slain.{{Fn|1c}}
