Erasmus Zachau.wikitext:
{{ImperiumPortal}}
'''Erasmus Zachau''' was a [[Necromunda (planet)|Necromunda]] [[Xenologist]], whose hunting of [[Underhive]] beasts led to the creation of the [[Principia Xenocarum]] [[Xenology (Imperium)|Xenology]] text.{{Fn|1}} 

Born a [[House Noble]] in [[Necromunda (planet)|Necromunda]]'s [[Hive Primus]], Zachau became a playboy and a dilettante who spent his days exploring its [[Underhive]]. He did so, to pose as a heroic slayer of beasts, similar to a mythological champion, but Zachau insisted on being accompanied by an entourage of servants while doing so. It was their job to record [[pict]] footage of the triumphs he had over the beasts of the Underhive. Later, as an older man, Zachau decided to employee an unnamed scholar to produce a book detailing every creature he had slain. The scholar managed to navigate Zachau's vainglorious boasting and produced a slender, but valuable, [[Xenology (Imperium)|Xenology]] text known as the [[Principia Xenocarum]].{{Fn|1}}  

