Ereden Adorjin.wikitext:
{{OrdoMalleusPortal}}
'''Ereden Adorjin'''{{Fn|1b}} was a [[Daemonhunter]] of the [[Ordo Malleus]] active in early [[M41]]. It is believed by the [[Inquisition]] that if her deeds were widely known, she would have been hailed as an [[Imperial Saint]].{{Fn|1a}}


==Biography==
Adorjin was born a [[psyker]], and early in her life she was consigned to the [[Black Ship]]s. However, unbeknownst to all aboard, the young Adorjin had been [[Daemonic Possession|possessed]] by a [[daemon]] known as [[Nekaybraianon]]. The daemon was brought onto the ship in her body and it was able to commit multiple atrocities on the psykers aboard the vessel on its way to [[Terra]]. However, with the help of [[Inquisitor]] [[Mardaine]], Adorjin was able to achieve the remarkable: she mustered the will required to unbind the daemon from her and cast it out.{{Fn|1a}}

With Mardaine as her mentor, Adorjin became an [[acolyte]] in service to the Ordo Malleus, eventually becoming an Inquisitor herself. Rather than sticking to a particular [[sector]] or region, Adorjin was a wandering Inquisitor. She started her career in [[Segmentum Solar]] and fought through into the [[Segmentum Pacificus]].{{Fn|1a}}

At the start of the [[Ninth Black Crusade]] of [[Abaddon|Abaddon the Despoiler]], Adorjin was selected as the next wielder of the legendary holy blade ''[[Luminous Reproach]]''.{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|Conflicting sources}}

Her hunt for Nekaybraianon lasted over two hundred years. On her journeys across the [[Imperium]] she was responsible for banishing dozens of powerful [[Daemon]]s and eradicating uncounted [[Chaos Cult|cults]]. She was also known to have fought alongside the legendary [[Grey Knights]] on so many occasions that an entire squadron of those warriors was assigned to aid her in her battles on a semi-permanent basis.{{Fn|1a}} She also possessed a copy of the ''[[Liber Daemonicum]]'', presented to her by [[Justicar]] [[Volze]].{{Fn|1b}}

Eventually in '''338.[[M41]]''' she was able to track Nekaybraianon down; the daemon had hoped to evade the Inquisitor's pursuit by possessing another psyker bound for the Black Ships, but Adorjin had seen through the daemon's plan by consulting the [[Emperor's Tarot]]. Using [[pentagrammic wards]] to seal Nekaybraianon on the ship, she confronted and battled the daemon and destroyed it with the ''Luminous Reproach''.{{Fn|1a}}  However, the psychic backlash of the monster's death killed everyone on board the ship and cast it into the [[Warp]], eventually becoming the core of a [[space hulk]] designated the ''[[Twilight]]''.{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|1c}}{{Fn|4}}

The last surviving data-file pertaining to Adorjin is a copy of a communique, believed to have been intended for one of her [[acolyte]]s, stored within an Inquisitorial archive. The message - her last words, for all intents and purposes - was ''"I've found him at last. His reckoning is long overdue. How fitting that it should end near exactly where it began."'' As the intended recipient was killed in a [[hive]] riot before they could elaborate on who or what Adorjin was referring to, the subject of the message remains a mystery, and there is no mention of her in any Imperial archives afterwards.{{Fn|1a}}

