Estrael (Adeptus Custodes).wikitext:
{{AdeptusCustodesPortal}}
'''Estrael''' was an [[Adeptus Custodes]] [[Hetaeron Guard|Hetaeron Companion]] and was among its forces that took part in the [[Horus Heresy]]'s [[Siege of Terra]].{{Fn|1b}}
==History==
Near the end of the [[Siege of Terra|Siege]], he was chosen to join the [[Emperor]]'s [[teleportation]] attack upon the traitorous [[Warmaster]] [[Horus]]' flagship, the [[Vengeful Spirit]]. Estrael was placed in Proconsul [[Caecaltus Dusk]]'s [[Shield Company]] which was to act as the Emperor's bodyguards during the battle with the [[Traitor]]s. However disaster struck, when their teleportation went awry and separated the Emperor and Dusk's Shield Company from the other [[Imperial]] forces now aboard the Vengeful Spirit.{{Fn|1a}} 

This was done by [[Horus]]' will and the [[Warmaster]] then used the power of [[Chaos]], to convince the [[Custodes]] that the [[Emperor]] was a corrupt monster and must die at their hands order to save the [[Imperium]]. Blood than began to pour from their eyes and while some were able to resist Horus and collapsed afterwards, many of the [[Shield Company]] turned on their Lord and began attacking Him. Though some of these Custodes were aware of what was going on, they could not stop themselves and the Emperor was forced to kill them in order to defend Himself{{Fn|1a}}. 39 would die at the Emperor's hands{{Fn|1b}}, before He was finally able to dispel Horus' Warpcraft with His [[psychic]] powers{{Fn|1a}}. Estrael was among the survivors and was one of the 28 Custodes who were able to stand by the Emperor, when He ordered them to rise. Those who could not were quickly killed by their Lord, with a psychic attack that caused a fatal cataclysmic intracerebral haemorrhage. However when the Emperor and the remaining Custodes began to enter one of the [[Vengeful Spirit]]'s hallways, Estrael began to moan. It was fully corrupted by the power of Chaos and the sight caused the [[Hetaeron Guard|Hetaeron Companion]] to submit once more to Horus' control. The Emperor was quick to act though and delivered the same fatal psychic attack to Estrael, as he had just done to the other prone Custodes.{{Fn|1b}}

