Etrus.wikitext:
{{ImperialFistsPortal}}
'''Etrus''' is a dour [[Imperial Fists]] [[Terminator]], who is accustomed to the stoic defensive tactics and endless firing drills favored by his [[Chapter]].{{Fn|1b}}

==History==
His [[Chapter]]'s training has made him a great marksman, and Etrus has received many honors for his accomplishments. It is only in battle that he comes alive, though, as Etrus revels in the destruction his [[Assault Cannon]] can cause. In [[M42]], Etrus was among the [[Imperial Fists]]{{Fn|1b}} that defended the [[Imperium]]'s worlds in the [[Vertex Sector]]. When the vital world of [[Vertex (World)|Vertex]], suffered an [[Ork]] invasion{{Fn|1a}} the Imperial Fists{{Fn|1b}} and several [[Space Marine Chapter]]s came to its defence.{{Fn|1a}} Etrus would do battle with the invading Orks{{Fn|1b}}, but his mission changed when the [[Xenos]] found a weakness in the [[Hive City]] of '''Acastus'''' defences. It had been protected during the invasion by a [[Void Shield|Void Shield network]], which was projected from an armoured bunker designated '''Shield Generator Gamma-9'''. However the Orks would discover this and several hordes were sent to destroy it, so the Xenos could invade the Hive City.{{Fn|1a}} 

The [[Chapter]]s became aware of the danger{{Fn|1a}} and each sent a [[Terminator]] to protect the [[Void Shield|Shield Generator]]. Etrus was sent by the [[Imperial Fists]] to defend it and he was joined by the [[Blood Angel]] [[Terminator Sergeant|Sergeant]] [[Angelus (Blood Angels)|Angelus]], the [[Salamanders|Salamander]] [[Magmus]], [[Space Wolf]] [[Stormheart]] and the [[Ultramarine]] [[Lucian (Ultramarines)|Lucian]].{{Fn|1b}} Though they numbered only five, in the close confines of the armoured bunker, these Terminator-armoured warriors would be in their element. None would allow the Orks access to '''Shield Generator Gamma-9''', without a fierce battle.{{Fn|1a}} 

