Falerius.wikitext:
{{UltramarinesPortal}}
'''Falerius''' was an [[Ultramarines]] [[Space Marine Lieutenant|Lieutenant]], who served in the [[Indomitus Crusade]].{{Fn|1}}

==History==
He was the second of the two [[Space Marine Lieutenant|Lieutenant]]s, who commanded a [[Space Marine Company|Company]] worth of [[Ultramarines]] sent to defend [[Cassothea]] during the [[Indomitus Crusade|Crusade]]. The world lays within the [[Pariah Nexus]] and was being invaded by hordes of [[Necron]], which vastly outnumbered the Ultramarines. Though the Crusade's command had ordered that Cassothea could not fall to the [[Xenos]], the war went badly quickly. Within only days of arriving there, the senior [[Space Marine Lieutenant|Lieutenant]] leading the Company was killed by the Necrons and Falerius took command of the Company. He ordered the Ultramarines to focus on saving Cassothea's capital city, '''Macuth''', but months later, the Necron had destroyed most of it. Many of the city's population had been massacred as well, along with over half of the Ultramarines. With no way to stop the Necron hordes from repairing themselves and with the last Crusade supply ship crashing into Cassothea, the order was given to evacuate the world. Soon afterwards, however, Falerius would go to aid one of his squadrons being pinned down by the Necron's fire. While his efforts ensured they escaped, several of the [[Xenos]]' [[Deathmark]]s had been lying in wait nearby for him and killed Falerius. Before his death, the Lieutenant had told [[Chaplain]] [[Sisenna]], that he wanted [[Space Marine Sergeant|Sergeant]] [[Allectius]] to succeed him, despite [[Fulgentius]] being the most senior of the Sergeants. While this went against the [[Codex Astartes]], the remaining Sergeants agreed to abide by Falerius' wishes - much to the shock of Allectius.{{Fn|1}} 

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Nexus (Novella)]], Chapter 1

