'''Fallon''' is a [[Blood Angels]] [[Death Company Chaplain]], who is a former protege of [[Lemartes]], the [[Chapter]]'s [[Death Company|Guardian of the Lost]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
In battle, Fallon always leads from the front of his [[Death Company]] charges and is seen as an icon for the blessings of the [[Blood Angels]]' [[Primarch]] [[Sanguinius]]' blood, as well as [[Red Thirst|the]] [[Black Rage|curses]] of the [[Chapter]]'s [[Gene-seed]]. He has taken part in the [[Surtellan Campaign]]{{Fn|1}} and the [[Dark Crusade (Imperium)|Dark Crusade]]'s{{Fn|2}} [[Mont'shi Campaign]], which was launched against the invading [[T'au Empire]].{{Fn|3}} During the conflict, Fallon led his [[Chapter]]'s forces in scouring the [[Mordant Zone]] of the [[Xenos]]. He then pushed into the [[Damocles Gulf]], where the [[Death Company Chaplain|Chaplain]] continued to fight the T'au.{{Fn|1}} Though the Mont'shi Campaign eventually ended in failure for the Imperium,{{Fn|2}} Fallon survived the Crusade.{{Fn|1}}
==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
''Fallon'', the [[Surtellan Campaign]] and the [[Mordant Zone]] were created for the [[Dark Crusade Campaign]], by the '''Hobby Center''' staff of [[Games Workshop]]'s '''Natick Mall''' store{{Fn|1}} in '''Natick, Massachusetts, USA'''.{{Fn|3}}

