Felicita.wikitext:
{{AdeptaSororitasPortal}}{{KhornePortal}}
'''Felicita''' is a [[Canoness]] of the [[Order of Our Martyred Lady]] and is among the forces of [[Indomitus Crusade Fleet Quartus]]'s [[Battle Group Jovia]] that have been corrupted by [[Khorne]]'s [[Murder-Curse]].{{Fn|1}} 
==History==
Among her [[Order of Our Martyred Lady|Order]]'s forces that served under her, were the [[Adepta Sororitas|Sisters]] [[Helenica]] and [[Kerenna]], who had an eye for the ebb and flow of battle. Felicita made note of this ability and claimed that Kerenna could one day succeed her as [[Canoness]] because of it. They both served in [[Battle Group Jovia|Jovia]]'s '''Task Force IX''', when it was sent to reclaim the [[Imperium Sanctus]] world [[Garvetha Primus]] and its [[system]] from [[Heretics]]. The Task Force invaded the world and soon only needed to conquer the city of '''Deng-Var''', to make Garvetha Primus' the [[Imperium]]'s once more. This would then allow the world's system to be opened up for further invasions. However it was as they were fighting to take back the city, that the [[Daemon Primarch]] [[Angron]] destroyed the [[Choral Engine]] on the [[Imperium Nihilus]] world [[Malakbael]], which the majority of [[Indomitus Crusade Fleet Quartus|Fleet Quartus]]' forces had been defending. The [[psychic]] beacon's subsequent explosion, then unleashed [[Khorne]]'s [[Murder-Curse]] [[Warp]] plague, within Malakbael's [[Malak System|system]]. However due to its Battle Groups sharing psychic channels with each other, the Murder-Curse was able to spread to them all, no matter where they were located within the [[Galaxy]].{{Fn|1}}  

Because of this, the [[Warp]] plague soon reached '''Task Force IX''' and those who were infected by it, immediately became servants of the [[Khorne|Blood God]]. Now filled with murderous bloodlust and rage, they then fell upon anyone that was near them, including their former allies. While [[Kerenna]] was able to resist the [[Murder-Curse]], Felicita became corrupted by it and grew horns from her eye sockets and developed a mouth filled of needle-like fangs.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Arks of Omen: Angron]], pgs. 46-49 

