Felstorm.wikitext:
{{ImperialNavyPortal}}
'''Felstorm''' was a [[Imperial Navy Captain|Captain]] of the [[Imperial Navy]], active in late [[M39]].{{Fn|1}}


==History==
In [[980.M39]] Felstorm was in command of the Navy vessel ''[[Indomitable Presence]]''.  He accompanied [[Inquisitor]] [[Daska]] on a mission in the [[Cloras System]] to survey the [[Space Hulk]] ''[[Unholy Harbinger]]''.{{Fn|1}}

In the depths of the Hulk, the Imperials found a dense mass of [[Living metal|unidentifiable metal]].  Although the substance defied [[augur]] analysis, the ''Indomitable Presence's'' database contained a report of a similar substance found in an [[Xenos|alien]] ruin on [[Tamar IV]].  Daska was able to access further reports that led him to restrict access to the Hulk while he conducted experiments on the mass.{{Fn|1}}

After some time, Daska reactivated power generators aboard the ''Unholy Harbinger'' to supply the metal mass with energy.  The metal started to expand and reform into a [[Eternity Gate (Necron)|platform holding a portal]] from which emerged [[Necron|metal monsters]] that slaughtered the Inquisitor's party.  Felstorm was forced to destroy the Hulk, launching salvo after salvo of [[torpedo]]es from the ''Indomitable Presence'' until it was reduced to wreckage strewn about the [[system]].{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
