Feron (Imperial Fists).wikitext:
{{ImperialFistsPortal}}
{{QuoteBox
|quote = '''''"I may not yet have the glorious power of a full [[Space Marine]], but let no man doubt my resolve or my mettle. What I do now... and in the future... I do for the [[Imperial Fists]], in the name of the [[Emperor]]. Glory walk with us all [[Battle Brothers|Brothers]]."'''<br>- Feron'''''{{Fn|1}}
|align = center
|width = 30em
}}
'''Feron''' is a [[Scout]] in the [[Imperial Fists]] [[Chapter]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
[[Image:Feron.jpg|thumb|200px|Feron{{Fn|1}}]]
He is among its forces fighting an [[Ork]] invasion on [[Kolkun]], where they are holding their battle line in the world's  '''Pumice Oceans''' desert. Feron was charged with data-gathering the Orks' gunnery positions in the Oceans' '''Tarkoom Flats''', for a major operation the Imperial Fists were launching against the [[Xenos]] the next day, when the sky lit up from a battle two miles away from him. From listing to his [[Vox]], the [[Scout]] learned that one of his Chapter's [[Attack Bike Squadron]]s had been attacked by the Orks. When he learned his [[Battle Brothers]] were pinned down and dying at the [[Xenos]]' hands, Feron rushed to aid them and tracked their location through the squad's life signals. Soon only one life signal remained active and the Imperial Fists in the area were also ordered to withdraw, due to Chapter's forces suffering heavy losses from the Orks' attacks. Feron refused to do so, however, and continued to kill or escape from the Xenos, as he tracked down the location of the remaining Attack Bike squadron member who was still alive.{{Fn|1}} 

The [[Scout]]'s search led him to infiltrate one of the [[Xenos]]' camps, where he found an [[Apothecary]] who had been tortured and strung up by the [[Orks]]. After killing the Xenos guards nearby, Feron freed the Apothecary and attempted to escape with him. However the Apothecary had been badly wounded and when he learned that only the Scout had arrived to save him, he stopped Feron. The Apothecary thanked the Scout for helping him, but noted that with his injuries it would be impossible for the two of them to escape. In truth, the Apothecary had only been willing himself to live in hopes that the Imperial Fists would recover the [[Cryo-Box]] he had stored his slain squadron's [[Gene-seed]] in. He stated that the Chapter could not afford to lose that much Gene-seed and tasked Feron with saving it. The Apothecary then told the Scout to take his bike in order to escape the Ork base, which the Xenos had stored nearby alongside the Cryo-Box. Once Feron agreed to do so and promised he would not fail, the Scout fulfilled the Apothecary's final request and granted his dying Battle Brother, the [[Emperor's Peace]]. With the Orks being alerted to his presence, Feron quickly booby-trapped the Apothecary's body with explosives, before he made his escape with the Cryo-Box. With the speed of the Apothecary's bike, he succeeded in doing so and his trap then exploded, killing several Orks, as Feron drove off to reunite with the Imperial Fists.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Flames of Damnation (Comic Anthology)]] — ''Last Man Standing''

