Freikstorn Strix.wikitext:
{{NecromundaPortal}}
'''Freikstorn Strix''' is a [[Necromunda (Planet)|Necromundan]] [[bounty hunter]] who is an exile of [[House Van Saar]], where he was once an [[archeotek]].{{Fn|1}}

==Biography==
[[file:Strix.jpg|thumb|right|200px|{{PAGENAME}}{{Fn|1}}]]
By his house's standards, Strix is ancient at the age of 47, but he has only achieved this by converting his [[survival suit|bodysuit]] into an armoured life-support cradle and by replacing his limbs with [[Imperial bionics|powerful cybernetics]], although he does not possess any of the [[archaeo-cyberteknika]] his former house is known for and that most archeoteks have at least some implants of. He created many of his body modifications by mixing Van Saar's [[STC]] technologies with common [[Imperial]] tech, but Strix must now harvest parts from his enemies in order to keep himself alive. This has led the bounty hunter to work with [[Underhive]] [[gang]]s if there is the promise of technology or a hefty score of creds.{{Fn|1}}

In combat, Strix is a deadly enemy, as he wields a "pneumatic-claw gun" (a harpoon launcher) and his bodysuit includes a jet pack he calls the S.H.O.C.K. (Strixian Harness and Ornithoptical Combat Kit) wing, which allows the bounty hunter to "soar" across the battlefield, although they don't allow true flight as [[yeld wings]] do. Perhaps the most deadly weapon he wields, though, is the fear Strix creates in his foes. Many of them believe the bounty hunter is not even [[human]] at all, but instead a mechanical horror that [[Hive Primus]]'s [[noble houses]] have unleashed upon the Underhive for their own dark amusement.{{Fn|1}}

==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
*The character's name may be a reference to the [[Wikipedia:Strix (mythology)|Strix]], owl-like birds of Roman mythology that were said to feed on human flesh.
*In addition, the character's backstory and design share some similarities with the Marvel Comics villain [[Wikipedia:Vulture (Marvel Comics)|Adrian Toomes]], a.k.a. The Vulture, an old man who wears a powered suit that allows him to fly and drain the life-force of his victims. 

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Necromunda: The Book of Peril]], pg. 31

