Fulgor Sagramoso.wikitext:
'''Fulgor Sagramoso''' was the traitorous [[Planetary Governor]] of [[Karkason (Mining World)|Karkason]], who seceded from the [[Imperium]].{{Fn|1a}}
==History==
He was a member of the [[Sagramoso Clan]], who had been the loyal rulers of [[Karkason (Mining World)|Karkason]] for thousands of years. This ended, though, when Fulgor became the world's [[Planetary Governor]] and declare himself to be an independent sovereign ruler and a god. He would now have control of his volcanic [[Mining World|Homeworld]]'s natural resources and would determine who they were sold to. While Fulgor was open to having a trade pact with the [[Imperium]] it would on his terms, a treaty of one god with [[Emperor|another]]. Then to prove his divinity to Karkason's people, Fulgor had its [[Preachers]] killed, and forced them to worship him and not the Emperor. Fulgor also had the world's [[Administratum]] officials killed, ensuring the Imperium was unaware of his acts. This led him to have full control of Karkason and as the years passed he sought to create an empire of his own. Fulgor began to seduce several Governors, mainly from neighboring [[Agri World|agricultural]] Systems, to turn upon the Imperium. He urged them to kill their Preachers and swear fealty to him and not the distant Emperor{{Fn|1a}}. He even somehwo managed to obtain 7 [[Battle Titan]]s, which Fulgor used to defend his rule of Karkason.{{Fn|1b}}

It would be 20 years after Fulgor seceded, that the [[Imperium]] finally retaliated in the form of the [[Karkason Crusade]]{{Fn|1a}}. Despite the presence of the [[Battle Titan]]s, however, Fulgor's forces were defeated and he was killed when his escape ship was destroyed by one of the Crusade's warships.{{Fn|1c}}

