==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
*Fulgrim's name may derive from the Latin word ''Fulgur'', meaning electrifying, flashing, or dazzling. His title Phoenician is a term that can mean of the civilisation of Phoenicia, the mythical Phoenix, or the colour purple depending on the context.
*[[Serena D'Angelus]]'s painting of Fulgrim and his later entrapment within it are very likely a reference to the novel [[Wikipedia:The Picture of Dorian Gray|The Picture of Dorian Gray]], where the titular character owns a painting that ages instead of him, allowing Dorian to indulge in hedonism and excess.

==={{Endn|Conflicting sources}}===
*According to [[Index Astartes I]], Fulgrim did not attain the status of [[Daemon Prince]] until after the [[Horus Heresy]].{{Fn|1}} However, the novel ''[[Angel Exterminatus (Novel)|Angel Exterminatus]]'' has him achieving Daemonhood during the Heresy.{{Fn|5}}

