'''Gabriel''' was a [[Dark Angels Grand Master|Grand Master]] of the [[Dark Angels]] [[Chapter]]'s [[Deathwing]].


==Biography==
===Pandorax Campaign===
*{{Main|Pandorax Campaign}}
{{Spoiler|source=Pandorax (Novel)}}''
In 960.[[M41]] Gabriel led the Deathwing during the [[Pandorax Campaign]]. When the Dark Angels first entered the [[Pandorax System|system]], he and the entirety of the Deathwing [[teleport]]ed aboard the [[asteroid]] [[Malefus Murex]]; they cleansed it easily, finding no serious resistance. After that, Gabriel and the Deathwing teleported over to the ship ''[[Revenge]]'' to reinforce the [[Grey Knights]]. He and several others, including [[Balthasar]], immediately met with [[Kaldor Draigo]]. After being informed that the Grey Knights just needed to get close enough to the portal to seal it, Gabriel and his Deathwing cleared a path for the Grey Knights and then protected them once they started the ritual to close it. When Kaldor returned after being taken away by a [[Daemon Prince]] Gabriel, along with [[Azrael]] and [[Ezekiel]], spoke with him.{{Fn|2a}}

Later in the campaign Gabriel fought against the enemy at [[Mount Dhume]] with 30 of the Deathwing and several thousand [[Imperial Guard]]. After getting visual confirmation that [[Abaddon]] was leading the assault he immediately requested reinforcements.{{Fn|2b}}

===Death===
He was later killed during a boarding attack on the [[Space Hulk]] ''[[Charnel Shrine]]''. After Gabriel's death, [[Belial]] was chosen to be his successor.{{Fn|1}}

