Gaius Pollandus.wikitext:
{{UltramarinesPortal}}
'''Gaius Pollandus''' was a [[Primaris Space Marine]] of the [[Ultramarines]].{{Fn|1}}


==Biography==
Recruited from the world of [[Talassar]], Pollandus's entire youth was a brutal struggle and this aided him in his entry into the chapter as an [[Aspirant]]. He began his career in the [[10th Company (Ultramarines)|10th Company]] as a [[Space Marine Scout|Scout]], seeing his first action on [[Chorgon II]] against the [[Ork]]s. During the war on [[Thanax]], Pollandus's squad spent several months severing rebel supply lines in the planet's frozen polar reaches. By this point, the [[Neophyte]]'s body had accepted his [[Gene-Seed]] and as a result he was promoted to [[Reiver]] Squad Agamnus, first seeing action in this new force against the [[Thousand Sons]] on [[Hespian]]. While fighting against the [[T'au]] on the [[Eastern Fringe]] as part of Strike Force Callepsean, he landed a killing shot on an [[Ethereal]] as an [[Vanguard Infiltrator]]. This act saw him promoted to a full-fledged Battle-Brother of the [[9th Company (Ultramarines)|9th Company]].{{Fn|1}}

As part of the 9th, Pollandus learned much of wider battlefield strategy and inter-squad tactics, eventually joining an [[Eliminator Squad]] during the battle against the [[Necron]]s on a forgotten [[Tomb World]]. During this war, his sniper squad engaged in tense duels with Necron [[Deathmark]]s. However, they were pulled out and redirected to [[Macragge]] when [[Death Guard]] forces pushed through the [[Phyrae Cordon]] to threaten the [[Factory World]] of [[Vansor V]]. It was during this battle that Pollandus first saw use as a [[Hellblaster]], fighting through the [[Servitine Ambush]] and the [[Battle of the Iron Steppes]] in this capacity. However, during the great engagement on Vansor V known as the Forgemaw's Push that Pollandus' squad was all but wiped out and he and [[Space Marine Sergeant|Sergeant]] [[Daros]] faced a Death Guard [[Defiler]] alone. The duo were successful in bringing the creature low, though he overloaded his [[Plasma Gun]]'s [[Machine Spirit]] in the process and it took him months to recover from his injures. Afterwards, he was promoted into the ranks of the [[8th Company (Ultramarines)|8th Company]].{{Fn|1}}

Now an [[Incursor]], [[Chaplain]]s noted that Pollandus was now a burning well of hate and anger that needed these emotions expunged before he could join the Battle Companies. He was thus assigned to an [[Aggressor Squad]] as part of Strike Force Calistus as they struck out to break the Siege of [[Hastoria]] against the [[Iron Warriors]]. During two years of fighting Pollandus vented his hate and was promoted to an [[Inceptor]] and performed a beachhead operation that earned him the Honour of the Iron Blade. Afterwards he saw action as a [[Repulsor Executioner]] crewman and briefly reassumed his role as a [[Vanguard Space Marine]], pushing back the Orks of the [[Charadon Sector]]. His actions during the war allowed him the right to finally join an [[Intercessor Squad]], and in this role he hunted down the [[Night Lords]] terrorizing the [[Sanctimus System]], battled [[Tyranid]]s on [[Horthis' Bane]], and participated in a [[3rd Company (Ultramarines)|3rd Company]] assault upon the [[Chaos Knight]]s of [[House Ghast]]. Following this daring mission Pollandus became a Sergeant of the [[6th Company (Ultramarines)|6th Company]] and led a squad of reserve formations attached to [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Galenus]]' [[5th Company (Ultramarines)|5th Company]] as part of the [[Drakon Crusade]], where he lost an arm. Having fought in the much-reduced 5th Company for so long, Pollandus and his two surviving brothers were promoted permanently as Intercessor Sergeants.{{Fn|1}}

Pollandus continued to serve with distinction in the 5th Company for several decades, traveling from one war zone to the other. Eventually, he and his squad held a choke point in complex agri-caverns for six days and nights against endless waves of Tyranids. His performance during this battle saw him promoted to the [[1st Company (Ultramarines)|First Company]]. As part of the 1st he was part of a mission alongside the [[4th Company (Ultramarines)|4th Company]] against the [[Traitor Titan]] works on [[Agator]]. His last deployment was in the defence of the Medicarum world of [[Phaetos]] on the fringes of [[Ultramar]]. There, he fell while single-handedly holding back a Death Guard assault against the [[Apothecarion]]-Primus facility while the rest of his squad evacuated before being killed by [[Deathshroud Terminator]]s. His brothers launched a blistering assault to reclaim his body, and this has allowed him to be interred on his homeworld of Talassar. His armour and weapons were returned to the Chapter Armoury to await their next user.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Codex: Space Marines (8th Edition, 2nd Codex)]], pgs. 14-15

