Galen (Heretic).wikitext:
{{ChaosPortal}}
'''Galen''' was the [[Imperial Commander|Planetary Lord]] of the [[Imperial]] world [[Antirrum]] and also secretly a [[Heretic]].{{Fn|1}}

==History==
[[Image:Galen.jpg|thumb|right|200px|Galen{{Fn|1}}]]
He had been one for sometime and had amassed a hidden arcana of [[Chaos]] lore. Galen's heresy, later led him to aid the [[Chaos Lord]] [[Katallus]] in [[Fall of Antirrum|successfully conquering]] [[Antirrum]], in order to garner further rewards for himself. Though the world was now controlled by Katallus, the [[Space Wolves]] would arrive to reclaim Antirrum for the [[Imperium]]. The battle that followed began to go badly for Katallus, who then called for a meeting with Galen. The [[Imperial Commander|Planetary Lord]] was worried, however, that the Chaos Lord would place the blame for the state of the battle on him and then kill him for it.{{Fn|1}} 

[[Katallus]] would in fact accept Galen's excuses and allowed the [[Imperial Commander|Planetary Lord]] to keep his life. After Galen left the meeting, though, the [[Chaos Lord]] remarked that while he did not blame the Planetary Lord for the [[Space Wolves]]' success in the battle, he was going to have Galen's head served on a platter after they defeated the [[Space Marines]]. He was looking so forward to this in fact, that Katallus remarked that he already savored the rich taste of Galen's head. Though the Space Wolves later defeated the Chaos Lord's forces, Katallus and his surviving [[Chaos Warband|Warband]] were able to flee from the world. Galen's collected arcana was later found by the [[Imperium]], and 90 percent of it was destroyed afterwards, but there was no sign of what became of the [[Heretic]] [[Imperial Commander|Planetary Lord]].{{Fn|1}}

==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
*''Galen'', [[Katallus]] and [[Antirrum]] were created by [[Tom Lauten]] and his team at [[Bright Light Studios]] for [[Games Workshop]]. They appeared in [[White Dwarf 210 (UK)]]'s [[Inferno! 0]].{{Fn|1}}

