Ganlick.wikitext:
{{AstraMilitarumPortal}}
'''Ganlick''' (sometimes called ''''Lick''') was a [[Sergeant (Imperial Guard)|Sergeant]]{{Fn|1b}} of the [[7th Paragonian Super-heavy Tank Company]], active in the late 300's.[[M41]].{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|1b}}


==Biography==
By the time of the [[Kalidar War]], Ganlick had served aboard the [[Baneblade]] ''[[Mars Triumphant]]'' for 13 years.{{Fn|1d}} He was the tank's Second Gunner, operating the tank's [[demolisher cannon]].{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|1b}} He was also the backup driver for ''Mars Triumphant'' on those occasions where the tank's main driver, [[Outlanner]], was forced to leave the cockpit for a sleep cycle that required the tank to keep moving.{{Fn|1d}}

In '''328.397.M41''', the 7th Paragonian was stationed in [[Macaree's Tablelands]], the tanks powered down for reactor maintenance. However, an [[ork]] warband used a dust storm as cover to attack the [[Imperial]] positions. The crewmembers of the 7th's tanks who remained onboard during the maintenance cycle were forced to use the tank's small arms, in particular the sponson-mounted [[heavy bolter]]s, to prevent the tanks being boarded by orks, with Ganlick manning ''Mars Triumphant's'' alongside [[Marsello]]. When [[Lieutenant (Imperial Guard)|Lieutenant]] [[Colaron Vor Artem Lo Bannick|Bannick]] made it back onto ''Mars Triumphant'', he took over one of the sponsons, with Ganlick manning the tank's pintle-mounted [[heavy stubber]]. Despite the weight of fire, however, one of the orks made it to ''Mars Triumphant'', climbing onto the tank and throwing Ganlick overboard, although the gunner managed to survive with minor injuries.{{Fn|1c}}

==Appearance & Personality==
Ganlick was bald and extremely large for a tanker. He was also noted to be quite superstitious; although rather foul-mouthed, he never argued with anyone while onboard the tank, as he believed that the act might upset ''Mars Triumphant's'' [[machine spirit]].{{Fn|1b}}

