Gemael.wikitext:
{{AstraMilitarumPortal}}
'''Gemael''' was an [[Atraxian Regiments|Atraxian]] [[Colonel]] of [[Battlegroup Kalidar]].{{Fn|1b}}

==Biography==
Gemael was a hardline follower of the ''[[Tactica Imperium]]'', considering any deviation from its maxims (or at least his interpretation of them) as tantamount to [[heresy]]. During the [[Kalidar War]] he was vehement in his rejection of the notion that the enemy [[ork]]s (specifically [[Blood Axes]]) were capable of employing any sort of stealth tactics. It even got to the point that he sentenced several [[Guardsmen]] to death for suggesting that the orks were using stealth.{{Fn|1b}}

In '''328.397.[[M41]]''' one of the Battlegroup's divisions, including the [[Command Leviathan]] ''[[Magnificence (Leviathan)|Magnificence]]'', was stationed in [[Macaree's Tablelands]].{{Fn|1a}} Gemael was in charge of setting the Imperial camps nearby{{Fn|1b}} while a number of the Imperial officers were attending a function aboard the ''Magnificence''.{{Fn|1a}}

During the night, however, a warband of orks attacked the Imperial positions under the cover of a sandstorm.{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|1b}} Although they were driven off, they did significant damage to a number of super-heavy vehicles (including the ''Magnificence'' itself) and killed a number of Guardsmen (including at least four officers). In the aftermath of the attack, [[General|Captain-General]] [[Iskhandrian]] had disciplinary charges filed against Gemael, [[Ostilek]] and [[Tulligen]], citing their treasonous lack of adaptability as being responsible for Imperial losses.{{Fn|1b}}

