Gerad Ixion.wikitext:
{{UltramarinesPortal}}
'''Gerad Ixion''' is the current [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] of the [[Ultramarines]] [[Chapter|Chapter's]] [[7th Company (Ultramarines)|7th (Reserve) Company]] and [[Master (Space Marine)|Chief Victualler]].{{Fn|1}}

He is both an old soldier and noble patrician hero, who has been made hard and cold by the galaxy's many horrors. To his [[Space Marine Company|Company]], Ixion is also a stern and exacting taskmaster, who pushes those under his command to excel with their every breath and waking deed. The Captain recognizes that only through harsh discipline and nigh-unattainable standards, can he do his duty to his [[Emperor of Mankind|Emperor]], his [[Roboute Guilliman|Primarch]] and the [[Battle-Brothers]] under his command.{{Fn|1}}

==Biography==

Shortly before the [[Siege of Zalathras]], while [[Calgar]] was traveling around [[Ultramar]], Captain Ixion and 7th company were holding position 4 light years from [[Prandium]]. [[Calgar]] wanted him and 7th company to stay at full readiness.{{Fn|5a}} During the siege the [[Librarian]] traveling with [[Calgar]] was able to make contact with 7th company and request their aid, Ixion then headed to [[Zalathras]] with the Andronicus fleet.{{Fn|5b}} When he arrived in system Ixion made contact with [[Calgar]] over Vox, and informed him they'd be ready to deploy planetside in 6 hours. [[Calgar]] ordered him to not start landings until Calgar told him, since he wanted to kill the head [[Ork]] and break the [[Waaagh]]. He also ordered Ixion to commit an [[Exterminatus]] if the city was lost to the [[Orks]] which Ixion agreed to.{{Fn|5c}}. After the head [[Ork]] was killed Ixion was ordered to deploy planetside.{{Fn|5d}}

Ixion was part of an [[Ultramarines]] force lead by [[Marneus Calgar]] to the [[Vortengard spiral]]. While en route [[Chief Librarian]] [[Tigurius]] forwarded them a message about a [[Tyranid]] attack at [[Styxia Prime]]. A meeting was called to decide what to do on the [[Octavius]]. During the meeting [[Cassius]] raised objections to the consensus that they don't need to intervene, Ixion suggested that [[Cassius]]'s hatred of the Tyranids clouded his judgement, and he believed that they would be wasting their warriors lives for vanity. [[Calgar]] decided to have [[Cassius]] lead a task force to [[Styxia Prime]] while everyone else, including Ixion, was to continue to the [[Vortengard Spiral]].{{Fn|2}}

In 999.M41 he attended the trial of [[Uriel Ventris]].{{Fn|4}}

He is among the [[Pariah Crusade]]'s forces fighting to defend the [[Imperial]] world [[Paradyce III]] from an invasion by the [[Necrons]].{{Fn|3}}

