Gervhart.wikitext:
__NOTOC__
{{BlackTemplarsPortal}}
'''Gervhart''' was the [[High Marshal (Black Templars)|High Marshal]] of the [[Black Templars]] [[Chapter]], active around [[M37]] or [[M38]].{{Fn|2}}{{Fn|Note 1}}

Gervhart was not only a fierce warrior but also a master tactician and student of history (second only to the Chapter's archivists in his knowledge and understanding of the ancient days of the [[Imperium]]).{{citethis}} He had studied the ways of war of every Marshal since the time of [[Sigismund]] and was well versed in the most arcane weapons and wargear.{{Fn|1}}

==Biography==
While still a [[Marshal (Black Templars)|Marshal]], Gervhart was the leader who initiated the [[Second Purging of Lastrati]].{{Cite this}}

He was also responsible for conducting the [[Athelor Crusade]]. While prosecuting this [[crusade]], he ordered the construction of [[Montgisard]], a chapter keep located on the planet [[Stygia XII]], which would serve the Chapter well for thousands of years before being abandoned.{{Fn|2}}


==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
===Notes===
*{{Endn|Note 1}}: [[Gideon Amesaris]], a [[Reclusiarch]] of the Black Templars who served under Gervhart, was stated by [[Chaplain]] [[Mathias Vlain]] to have had a hand in constructing one of the vaults beneath Montgisard ''"almost four thousand years ago"'' in the short story [[And They Shall Know No Fear... (Short Story)|And They Shall Know No Fear...]], which is set in 832.M41. This would imply that Gideon (and by extension Gervhart) served during late M37 or possibly early [[M38]].{{Fn|2}}

